@startuml
title CPU V3 revision 0.7 hardware structure

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

package "Fitted CPU V3 system (optional around the reusable core)" {
  component "Instruction cache\n2 KiB, direct mapped\n64 sets x 16 words\nwrite-through data RAM shape" as ICache
  component "Data cache\n2 KiB, direct mapped\n64 sets x 16 words\nwrite-through, no-write-allocate" as DCache
  component "Memory arbiter\nsingle outstanding owner" as Arbiter
  component "SDRAM word/line adapter\n22-bit fitted physical word address" as SDRAM
  component "Devices 0..7\n16 channels each" as Devices
  component "DMA / display\noptional system masters" as Masters
}

rectangle "CpuV3Core: blocking, in-order, one instruction in flight" as Core {
  component "Fetch / execute FSM\nrequest -> response -> execute\nprecise single retirement" as FSM
  storage "Instruction state\nPC 16, CSEG 16, DSEG 16\nIMMHI12 prefix\npending comparison" as ControlState
  storage "GPR file\n16 x 16-bit\ncombinational read\nsynchronous write" as GPR
  component "Integer lane\n16-bit ALU, shifts, compare\nCLZ / popcount" as IntAlu
  component "Integer multiplier\nregistered signed 18 x 18 DSP\n2-stage primitive" as IntDsp

  package "Blocking fix16 FPU" {
    storage "FPR file\n16 x (4 x signed Q8.8)\n64 x 16-bit RAM16\n2 registered-address async reads\n1 synchronous write" as FPR
    component "Serialized vector lane\n17-bit saturated add/sub\nABS/NEG/FLOOR/CEIL/ROUND\nSAT01/SIGN and lane moves" as LaneAlu
    component "FPU multiplier\nregistered signed 18 x 18 DSP\n1 lane, 2-stage primitive\nnearest-even writeback" as FpuDsp
    database "Shared unary ROM\n1024 x 16-bit BSRAM\n256 sin + 256 rcp + 512 rsqrt" as Rom
    component "Unary normalize / scale\nlatched domain + exponent\nregistered normalized mantissa\nshared 17-bit round shifter\nregistered scale result" as Unary
    storage "ACC\nsigned 40-bit\nper-product saturation" as Acc
    storage "Transfer / snapshot state\n4 x 16-bit buffer\ntranspose swap registers" as Transfer
    component "FPU phase controller\nblocking until commit or fault\nfixed four-lane execution today" as FpuFsm
  }
}

ICache --> FSM : instruction ready/valid
FSM --> ICache : 32-bit {CSEG, PC}
DCache --> FSM : data response
FSM --> DCache : 32-bit {DSEG, offset}\n16-bit narrow requests
FSM <--> Devices : dedicated device port
ICache --> Arbiter
DCache --> Arbiter
Masters --> Arbiter
Arbiter --> SDRAM
Masters ..> ICache : invalidate / snoop
Masters ..> DCache : invalidate / snoop

FSM <--> ControlState
FSM <--> GPR
GPR --> IntAlu
IntAlu --> GPR
GPR --> IntDsp
IntDsp --> GPR
FSM --> FpuFsm : opcode D dispatch
FpuFsm --> FSM : one precise retire / fault
GPR --> FpuFsm : scalar and address
FpuFsm --> GPR : FSTORE
FPR --> LaneAlu : one lane from each read port
LaneAlu --> FPR : registered serial write
FPR --> FpuDsp
FpuDsp --> FPR
FpuDsp --> Acc
Acc --> FPR : FACCSTORE
FPR --> Unary
Unary --> Rom : 10-bit address
Rom --> Unary : synchronous table word
Unary --> FPR
FPR <--> Transfer
Transfer <--> DCache : four sequential beats

note right of FpuFsm
Current issue policy:
* no CPU/FPU overlap
* no cross-instruction pipeline
* add/move/simple unary: one overlapped lane per cycle
* multiply/dot: one tagged DSP issue/result per cycle after fill
* continuation k early-exit is not implemented
end note

note bottom of Core
Core target-leaf resources:
* integer multiplier: 1 MULT18X18 lane
* FPU multiplier: 1 MULT18X18 lane
* FPU unary table: 1 x 1024x16 BSRAM
* FPR leaf claim: 40 RAM16 cells
  (32 for two read copies + 8 characterized incidental cells)
The system composes these claims with cache, boot, display, and board resources.
end note

@enduml
